      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Route performance highlights and checkpost advisory for the Mumbai‑Coimbatore corridor</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><div style="background: rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.08); border-left: 4px solid #f59e0b; border-radius: 0 10px 10px 0; padding: 18px 22px; margin: 24px 0;"><h4 style="color: #f59e0b; font-size: 1.05rem; font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 6px 0;"><i class="fas fa-exclamation-triangle" style="margin-right: 8px;"></i>Important Logistics Advisory</h4><div style="color: #cbd5e1; font-size: 0.92rem; margin: 0; line-height: 1.6;"><strong>Mumbai‑Coimbatore route</strong> performance highlight and checkpoint advisory</div></div>
<h3>Average Transit Speed</h3>
<p>Freight operators report a consistent average speed of <strong>55–60 km/h</strong> on the Mumbai‑Coimbatore corridor, factoring in highway stretches, urban bottlenecks, and scheduled stops. During peak monsoon months, speeds may dip to 45 km/h, while dry season runs often sustain the upper range.</p>
<h3>Key Checkpoints</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>NH 48 – Mumbai to Pune (Km 0‑150)</strong>: Toll plaza at Khandala, mandatory weigh‑in at Pune depot.</li>
<li><strong>NH 48 – Pune to Satara (Km 151‑300)</strong>: Checkpoint at Satara for emissions verification.</li>
<li><strong>NH 48 – Satara to Kolhapur (Km 301‑460)</strong>: Toll plaza at Kolhapur; security inspection for hazardous cargo.</li>
<li><strong>NH 48 – Kolhapur to Belgaum (Km 461‑620)</strong>: Border checkpoint for Karnataka state tax compliance.</li>
<li><strong>NH 48 – Belgaum to Hubli (Km 621‑720)</strong>: Toll plaza at Hubli; optional rest stop for driver fatigue management.</li>
<li><strong>NH 48 – Hubli to Bangalore (Km 721‑950)</strong>: Multiple weigh‑stations; high‑traffic area near Bangalore outskirts.</li>
<li><strong>NH 48 – Bangalore to Salem (Km 951‑1150)</strong>: Toll plaza at Salem; checkpoint for cargo documentation.</li>
<li><strong>NH 44 – Salem to Coimbatore (Km 1151‑1300)</strong>: Final toll at Coimbatore; customs clearance for cross‑state freight.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Toll Considerations</h3>
<p>Expect a total toll expense of <strong>₹3,200–₹3,800</strong> for a fully loaded truck, varying with vehicle class and axle count. Pre‑pay options via FASTag reduce queue time by up to 40% at each plaza. Keep a digital copy of the FASTag transaction log for audit purposes.</p>
<h3>Tips to Avoid Delays</h3>
<ul>
<li>Plan departures early in the morning to bypass peak city traffic in Mumbai and Bangalore.</li>
<li>Monitor real‑time traffic updates on the NHAI portal; reroute around construction zones near Pune and Salem.</li>
<li>Maintain a valid FASTag and ensure sufficient balance before entering toll zones.</li>
<li>Schedule mandatory weigh‑ins during off‑peak hours to minimize wait times.</li>
<li>Carry all required documentation (e‑way bill, insurance, and vehicle permits) in both physical and electronic formats.</li>
<li>Utilize rest stops strategically for driver fatigue; a 30‑minute break every 4 hours improves safety and compliance.</li>
</ul>
<p>By adhering to these guidelines, operators can maximize efficiency on the Mumbai‑Coimbatore route, ensuring timely deliveries and reduced operational costs.</p></div>
